{"id":"word:hebrew:H349","type":"word","title":"אֵיךְ","subtitle":"H349 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"how? or how! ; also where","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אֵיךְ (H349) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: adv.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 82 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אֵיךְ (ʼêyk) means how? or how! ; also where First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 12 6."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אֵיךְ","transliteration":"ʼêyk","pronunciation":"ake","strong":"H349","lemmaId":"hebrew:H349","partOfSpeech":"adv","forms":["אֵ֚יךְ","אֵ֣יךְ","אֵיכָ֥ה","וְ/אֵ֥יךְ","וְ/אֵ֖יךְ"],"morphs":[["HTi",63],["HC/Ti",19]]},"definitions":{"short":"how? or how! ; also where","usage":"how, what.","full":"H349. ek אֵיךְ 59 (Aramaic אֵיךְ , [pronounced âch ]) adverb 1. interrogative How? Gen 26:9 ; 2Sam 1:5 , 14 ; 1Kin 12:6 ; Isa 20:6 and elsewhere; often with imperfect (especially in 1 person) in an expostulation Gen 39:9 ; 44:8 , 34 ; Josh 9:7 ; 2Sam 2:22 ; 12:18 ; Psa 137:4 ; Isa 48:11 for how should it be profaned ? תאמר(וׅ איך how canst or dost thou (do you) say . . . ? Judg 16:15 ; Isa 19:11 ; Jer 2:23 (compare 8:8 אֵיכָה ) 48:14 ; Psa 11:1 ; in an indirect sentence 2Kin 17:28 ; Jer 36:17 ; Ruth 3:18 . 2. as an exclamation How! whether of lamentation 2Sam 1:19 ; Jer 2:21 ; 9:18 ; Micah 2:4 ; or of satisfaction Isa 14:4 , 12 ; Jer 48:39 ; 51:41 ; Obadiah 5 and elsewhere; with intensive force = how gladly! 3:19 , how terribly! 9:6 (but others render here 'for how [else] should I do'? etc.) ** Hosea 11:8 according to Hi Ke We Marti and others. אֵיכָה (from אַי and כָּה = כֹּה ; compare Assyrian ekiam ) adverb 1. interrogative In what manner? τίνι τρόπῳ ; (rather more definite than אֵיח = πῶς ); Deut 1:12 ; 7:17 ; 12:30 ; 18:21 ; 32:30 ; Judg 20:3 (indirect sentence) 2Kin 6:15 ; Jer 8:8 ; Psa 73:11 . 2 exclamation How! (slightly more emphatic than אֵיח ) Isa 1:21 ; Jer 48:17 ; Lam 1:1 ; 2:1 ; 4:1-2 ,. 3 Where? (properly north-Israel; compare Aramaic אֵיכָא , where ? compare Dr Intr. 178, 421 ) only 2Kin 6:13 Kt Song 1:7 (twice in verse), &#8212; each time in an indirect sentence. אֵיכָ֫כָה (Canticles) ֵאיכָכָ֫ה (Esther) (from אַי & כָּ֫כָה thus ) How ? only Song 5:3 (twice in verse); Est 8:6 (twice in verse).","rootNote":"also אֵיכָה ; and אֵיכָכָה ; prolonged from 335 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 12 6","keyReferences":["1Kgs 12 6","1Sam 16 2","2Chr 10 6","2Kgs 6 15","2Kgs 10 4","2Kgs 17 28","2Kgs 18 24","2Sam 1 5"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":82,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 12 6","book":"1Kgs","chapter":12,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵ֚יךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTi"},{"reference":"1Sam 16 2","book":"1Sam","chapter":16,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵ֣יךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTi"},{"reference":"2Chr 10 6","book":"2Chr","chapter":10,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵ֚יךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTi"},{"reference":"2Kgs 6 15","book":"2Kgs","chapter":6,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵיכָ֥ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTi"},{"reference":"2Kgs 10 4","book":"2Kgs","chapter":10,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/אֵ֖יךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ti"},{"reference":"2Kgs 17 28","book":"2Kgs","chapter":17,"verse":28,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵ֖יךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTi"},{"reference":"2Kgs 18 24","book":"2Kgs","chapter":18,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/אֵ֣יךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ti"},{"reference":"2Sam 1 5","book":"2Sam","chapter":1,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵ֣יךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTi"},{"reference":"2Sam 1 14","book":"2Sam","chapter":1,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵ֚יךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTi"},{"reference":"2Sam 1 19","book":"2Sa